        "subject": "Woodwork",
        "topic": "Timber Conversion Techniques",
        "question_text": "<p>Which timber conversion method is most likely to produce the least waste and is commonly used for valuable hardwoods?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The <i>quarter-sawing</i> method involves cutting the log radially into quarters and then sawing each quarter perpendicular to the growth rings. This method produces less waste, enhances the appearance of the grain, and reduces warping, making it ideal for valuable hardwoods.</p>",
